Translation patch: `compress_with`, `CompData::write_payload`, `PacketCodecInner::compress` (src/proto/codec): route flate2 through `codec::trusted`

Change: (a) `compress_with`: `compression != Compression::none()` becomes `!trusted::compression_eq(compression, trusted::compression_none())`; `deflater.get_or_insert_with(|| Compress::new(compression, true))` followed by `deflate_into(deflater, chunk, dst)?` becomes a `match deflater`: `Some(d)` deflates with `d`; `None` creates `trusted::compress_new(compression)`, deflates with it, stores it in `*deflater`, then applies `?`. The compressed branch writes the header with the same `put_uint_le`/`put_u8` calls and then `dst.put_slice(&compressed)` in place of `unsafe { .. dst.advance_mut(compressed_len) }`. (b) `CompData::write_payload`: the same `match` for the inflater (`trusted::decompress_new()`), `trusted::inflate(inflater, payload, plain_len)?` and then `dst.extend_from_slice(&plain)`. (c) `PacketCodecInner::compress`: `c.level != level` becomes `!trusted::compression_eq(c.level, level)`. (d) `deflate_into`/`inflate_into` are removed (now unused), and the now test-only import `FlushCompress` is `#[cfg(test)]`.
Why: Aeneas does not support closures as values (`get_or_insert_with`), `unsafe` writes into spare capacity, or flate2; see patch 120.
Behaviour: Identical.
  - The `match` does what `get_or_insert_with` does: it inserts a new stream only when `None`, and the stream is stored before the `?`, as upstream (where it is inserted before deflating).
  - Upstream deflates into `dst.chunk_mut()[7..7 + chunk.len()]` (spare capacity reserved just before), writes the 7 header bytes in front of it with `put_uint_le`/`put_u8`, and exposes the deflated bytes with `advance_mut(compressed_len)`. `trusted::deflate` deflates the same input with the same stream, flush mode and output length into a fresh buffer and returns its first `compressed_len` bytes under the same condition (`StreamEnd && compressed_len < chunk.len()`), which are then appended after the same header: `dst` ends with the same bytes, and the stream's state is the same.
  - Upstream inflates into `dst.chunk_mut()[..plain_len]` and calls `advance_mut(plain_len)` only on success; `trusted::inflate` returns the same bytes (or the same error), which are appended on success only. On error `dst`'s bytes are unchanged in both. `dst.reserve(plain_len)` only changed the capacity.
  - `Compression` derives `PartialEq`, so `!=` is `!compression_eq`.

